1
00:00:00,522 --> 00:00:01,592
(Amy:)Do you know him?

2
00:00:01,591 --> 00:00:04,021
(Dave:)No, but I've followed
his work for years.

3
00:00:04,027 --> 00:00:05,197
(Dave:)He's a rock star.

4
00:00:05,195 --> 00:00:06,995
(Dave:)You've got to
tell me about him.

5
00:00:06,996 --> 00:00:08,796
(Dave:)What's he like?

6
00:00:11,133 --> 00:00:13,933
(door opens)
He really seems into her.

7
00:00:15,404 --> 00:00:17,204
(Bernadette:)I took a video.

8
00:00:17,207 --> 00:00:20,077
(Bernadette:)I forgot how much
fun this is.

9
00:00:20,076 --> 00:00:21,376
(Leonard:)Okay, we saw them.

10
00:00:21,377 --> 00:00:23,077
(Leonard:)Can we go catch the movie?

11
00:00:23,079 --> 00:00:25,149
(Penny sighs)
Why'd you bring him?

12
00:00:25,148 --> 00:00:27,748
(Penny:)I had to; we're married now.

13
00:00:27,750 --> 00:00:29,820
(Bernadette:)Ugh, I hear that.

14
00:00:35,555 --> 00:00:37,925
(Dave:)I'm sorry, just one more
question about Sheldon.

15
00:00:37,925 --> 00:00:40,025
(Amy:)Sure, why not?

16
00:00:40,027 --> 00:00:42,627
(Dave:)It's more of a four-part
question, really.

17
00:00:44,063 --> 00:00:46,603
(Dave:)When he wrote his paper on
supersingular prime numbers,

18
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:48,170
(Dave:)how long did it take?

19
00:00:49,002 --> 00:00:50,972
(Amy:)Um... about an hour and half.

20
00:00:50,971 --> 00:00:52,301
Wow!

21
00:00:53,807 --> 00:00:55,407
I mean, wow!

22
00:00:55,409 --> 00:00:57,409
(Dave:)And you were
there to see it?

23
00:00:57,411 --> 00:01:01,021
(Amy:)Yes. Yep. We were on a date.

